    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d375">

                <pb facs="0286" n="236" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg236"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/413</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-06-05T18:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">June 5, 1918, 6
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 5, 5.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your June 3, 4 p.m. Certainly I shall not leave my post as long as you think my
                    services will help. I want to be exceedingly frank and say that an attempt to
                    assist through the Soviet would be a serious mistake. All the reports from
                    Siberia confirm increasing weakness. Czech soldiers <hi rendition="#italic">en
                        route</hi> east now successfully fighting them and having [prevailed?] will
                    force their passage to the French front.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
